---
import InsertLayout from '../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/jsonld';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Policies', url: '/policies' }
]);

const lastUpdated = 'September 19, 2026';
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Service Policies"
  description="Scoping, delivery, cancellation, and support policies for Toledo Technologies software services."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="Service Policies"
  subheading={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`}
>
  <p>
    These are the website-level policies for service inquiries. A signed
    statement of work or project agreement controls when its terms differ from
    this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Current Offer</h2>
  <p>
    Toledo Technologies currently offers software discovery, implementation,
    repair, performance, and support services.
  </p>

  <h2>Scoping & Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The scope, deliverables, timeline, payment schedule, and acceptance terms
      are confirmed in writing before project work begins.
    </li>
    <li>
      Paid discovery products are due 100% upfront. When stated on the discovery
      page and project agreement, 50% of that fee can be credited to the kickoff
      Project Retainer for a qualifying engagement started within 30 days. The
      credit is capped at that Project Retainer; unused credit lapses and does
      not roll forward.
    </li>
    <li>
      The kickoff Project Retainer and later milestone terms depend on the
      signed project agreement; a website price guide is not an invoice or
      guarantee of scope.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fulfillment & Delivery</h2>
  <p>Delivery follows the written project scope and may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Repository access, commits, patches, or pull requests</li>
    <li>Decision records, technical plans, and handoff documentation</li>
    <li>Deployment or operating guidance when included in scope</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Delivery dates depend on the engagement and required client access. They are
    confirmed in the project agreement, not inferred from marketing copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation & Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Which refund terms apply depends on what was bought and where. The terms
    printed on the product page at the time of purchase are the ones in force.
    This section states them in one place.
  </p>

  <h3>Products bought directly from Toledo Technologies</h3>
  <p>
    These are one-off purchases made without a signed agreement. The window runs
    from the date of purchase, and no explanation is required where a window is
    stated.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Migration Acceptance Kit</strong> (single-organisation and
      consultancy licences) — full refund within 30 days. The same term is in
      the kit licence.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>AWS deprecation evidence report</strong> (eolkits.com) — full
      refund within 30 days. If automated delivery fails permanently, a full
      refund is issued without a request being needed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Downloads, field guides, and bundles</strong> on
      shop.toledotechnologies.com — full refund within 14 days, including files
      already downloaded. The shop's own refund page carries the full text.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Compliance kits and the vulnerability handling starter pack</strong>
      on cra.toledotechnologies.com — full refund within 14 days, returned
      through PayPal to the original payment method.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Occasion drafts</strong> on saiditright.com — full refund within
      7 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>podfreeze Pro licences</strong> — full refund within 30 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fixed-scope file conversion</strong> — refunded in full if we
      cannot read the file supplied, or if the work turns out to fall outside
      the scope printed on that product page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Integration triage</strong> — refunded in full if the reported
      failure cannot be reproduced.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Feed check</strong> — refunded in full if the feed cannot be
      fetched or is not in the format the offer states.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where a fixed-price product is not listed above, the refund condition
    printed on its own product page governs, and that condition is the whole of
    it. To ask for a refund, email <a href="mailto:hello@toledotechnologies.com"
      >hello@toledotechnologies.com</a
    > with the receipt or order reference. Approved refunds are returned to the
    original payment method; how long the credit takes to post is controlled by
    the payment provider and the card issuer.
  </p>

  <h3>Items sold by another merchant</h3>
  <p>
    Some Toledo Technologies products are sold through a merchant of record.
    That company is the seller for those orders, and its terms — not this page —
    govern the refund.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Gumroad</strong> — the guides and bundles listed at
      toledotechnologies.gumroad.com. Gumroad takes the payment and handles any
      refund under Gumroad's own terms. Refund requests go through Gumroad.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Polar</strong> — the Tessera PCI DSS evidence products. Polar
      takes the payment and handles any refund under Polar's own terms. Those
      products also issue a refund automatically when a paid item is not
      delivered; the Tessera refunds page states the conditions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Microsoft Store</strong> — Paulatim for Windows. Microsoft
      processes the purchase and any refund under Microsoft Store policy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Quoted engagements</h3>
  <p>
    Cancellation, pause, and refund terms are defined in the signed agreement.
    Unless that agreement says otherwise, completed work and approved expenses
    remain payable, and any unused prepaid amount is reconciled against work
    performed. Custom deliverables are not treated as returnable retail goods.
  </p>
  <p>
    If Toledo Technologies cannot deliver an agreed item, the parties will
    document a correction, replacement, scope adjustment, or refund of the
    applicable unused amount.
  </p>

  <h2>Support</h2>
  <p>
    Warranty periods, response targets, maintenance, and ongoing support exist
    only when written into the applicable agreement or Care plan. A project does
    not silently include indefinite support.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Ask a policy question at <a href="mailto:hello@toledotechnologies.com"
      >hello@toledotechnologies.com</a
    > or use the <a href="/contact?subject=Service%20policy%20question"
      >contact form</a
    >.
  </p>
</InsertLayout>
